{"id":"23f1dab6b25c9b7604502d7adf32f7e13c94bf09b5bf76380fa91bc1824f026b","lamport":0,"author":"scual.project@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-10-04T12:18:03.163651Z","format_version":1,"kind":"create","payload":{"fields":{"created-at":"2026-10-04T12:18:03.163651Z","created-by":"carlo.cifarelli@gmail.com","description":"Flagship step 4/6 of the op-log roadmap (parent 0e7b1245).\n\nAppend-only operation log under ticgit:tickets:<uuid>:ops:<lamport>:<hash> as the\nsynced, conflict-free source of truth (merge = union of op sets, replay in clock\norder). Current state keys become a rebuildable local cache with 3-tier staleness\ndetection (fresh / incremental replay / rebuild) keyed on cache:head. Ships the\n`ti verify` consistency oracle (replay full log, diff against cache).\n\nDepends on steps 1-3 (content IDs, versioning, forward-compat) so the format\nbreak is survivable. Full design in the parent ticket's spec.","parent":"0e7b1245-e860-4843-9df3-101cd9a0a746","priority":"2","spec":"# Spec — Op-log CRDT + derived cache (flagship)\n\nRoadmap step 4/6 (parent 0e7b12). Depends on steps 1 (content-ids), 2 (versioning),\n3 (forward-compat). This is the central change; see the parent ticket's spec for\nthe architecture-level rationale.\n\n## Goal\n\nReplace last-write-wins on scalar ticket fields with an append-only operation log\nas the conflict-free source of truth, and turn the current field keys into a\nrebuildable derived cache with staleness detection. Unlock free history and\npoint-in-time queries; `ti verify` as a consistency oracle.\n\n## Current state (what actually needs changing — narrower than it looks)\n\ngit-meta already gives us conflict-free merge for TWO of the three write shapes:\n\n| Write today | git-meta primitive | Merge behavior | Needs op-log? |\n|-------------|--------------------|----------------|---------------|\n| scalars (title, status, state, priority, assigned, milestone, points, code, parent, description, spec, created-*) | `p.set(key, val)` | **LWW clobber** | **YES** |\n| sets (tags, children, depends_on, blocks) | `p.set_add(key, val)` | union (already CRDT) | no |\n| comments | `p.list_push(key, json)` | append-only list | no |\n\nSo the flagship's real job is: **route scalar field mutations through ops**;\nset/list writes can stay as-is initially (they already converge). This sharply\nreduces scope and risk.\n\n## Operation log layout (`keys.rs`)\n\n    ticgit:tickets:<uuid>:ops:<lamport>:<hash>\n\n- `<lamport>` zero-padded fixed-width (e.g. 20 digits) so lexical prefix-scan\n  order == numeric order (consistent with the no-index, scan-everything model).\n- `<hash>` = content-id from step 1; tiebreaks equal Lamport values\n  deterministically.\n- Value = JSON op envelope (step 3 shape): `{id, kind, lamport, author,\n  created_at, format_version, payload}`.\n- Op kinds (initial): `create`, `set-field` (compound: `field → value` map),\n  `set-lifecycle`, `clear-field`. One op per user command (resolved decision #1\n  in parent spec), carrying all fields that command touched.\n\nAdd `keys.rs` helpers: `ticket_ops_prefix(id)`, `ticket_op(id, lamport, hash)`,\n`parse_ticket_op(key) -> Option<(Uuid, u64, &str)>`, plus `cache:head`.\n\n## Lamport clock (resolved decision #2)\n\n- No separate counter key. On append, the next Lamport = `max(seen) + 1` where\n  `max(seen)` is read from the op-key `<lamport>` components during the same scan\n  that builds the cache. `cache:head` memoizes the last-seen max so steady-state\n  appends don't rescan the whole op-space.\n- Concurrent equal-Lamport ops order by `<hash>`.\n\n## Derived cache + staleness\n\n- Cache = today's scalar field keys (`ticgit:tickets:<uuid>:<field>`), repurposed\n  as a disposable projection of the op-log, PLUS a `cache:head` recording the\n  (lamport, hash) of the last op folded in.\n- Read path (`load`/`list`): compare `cache:head` against the real op-log head:\n  - equal → use cache directly (zero replay).\n  - head ahead → replay only ops after `cache:head` (incremental fold), update cache.\n  - diverged (post-merge: an op exists with lamport ≤ head but unknown hash) →\n    rebuild that ticket's cache from scratch by full replay.\n- Replay = deterministic left-fold of ops in (lamport, hash) order into a\n  `Ticket` (reuse `build_ticket`'s folding as the projection target).\n\n## Cache placement — DECIDED 2026-10-04: local, gitignored\n\nThe cache is a LOCAL, gitignored build artifact (e.g. `.git/ticgit/cache`); only\nthe op-log syncs. Precedent: `session_state.rs` already stores local-only state.\nConsequence: the current `ticgit:tickets:<uuid>:<field>` scalar keys STOP being\nsynced truth — they become (or are mirrored by) the local cache projection, and\nthe op-log under `ops:` is the only synced scalar authority. The cache can never\nconflict, and push/pull shrink. This unblocks the write path below.\n\n## `ti verify` (consistency oracle)\n\n`commands/verify.rs`: replay the full op-log into a fresh projection and diff\nagainst the stored cache. Report drift / corruption / bad-migration per ticket.\n`--json` structured; non-zero exit on any mismatch. Cheap once the two layers\nexist; doubles as the migration's correctness net.\n\n## Write path\n\n- `store.rs` scalar setters (`set_title`, `set_state`, `set_lifecycle`,\n  `set_priority`, …) and `create` stop calling `p.set` directly; instead they\n  append a `set-field`/`set-lifecycle` op and update the cache in the same\n  transaction. Keep the public `TicketStore` method signatures unchanged so the\n  CLI and tests don't churn.\n- Sets/comments: unchanged for v1 (already convergent). A later step may move\n  them into ops for uniform history, but not required here.\n\n## Migration (resolved decision #3)\n\n`ti migrate` (step 2) synthesizes ONE snapshot `create` op per existing ticket\nfrom its current scalar fields (lamport 0, synthetic migration author), then\nwrites `cache:head`. No fabricated per-field history. Idempotent.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- CLI test: two clones edit DIFFERENT scalar fields of the same ticket, sync,\n  and BOTH edits survive (today one clobbers the other) — the headline win.\n- CLI test: two clones edit the SAME field; result is deterministic by\n  (lamport, hash) on both clones, and the losing value is recoverable from\n  `ti history`.\n- CLI test: `ti verify` passes on a healthy repo; detect-and-report on a\n  deliberately corrupted cache key.\n- Perf: `ti list` with a warm cache does zero replay (assert via instrumentation\n  or a replay counter in tests).\n- All existing ~48 CLI integration tests stay green (signatures unchanged).\n\n## Risks\n\n- Biggest risk is the write path touching every setter; mitigate by keeping\n  method signatures stable and landing behind the step-2 version bump so rollback\n  is a documented migration, not a break.\n- Cache-placement decision must be made first (see above).\n\n## Decisions locked 2026-10-04 (cutover)\n\nCLEAN CUTOVER. On migration the on-disk ticket format bumps to **2**:\n- `ti migrate` v1→v2 converts each ticket's current scalar keys into a single\n  snapshot `create` op (lamport 0, synthetic migration author) and REMOVES the\n  legacy synced scalar keys.\n- The writer thereafter syncs ONLY ops for scalar fields (+ the local cache);\n  it no longer writes synced scalar keys. Sets/comments unchanged (already\n  convergent).\n- Old binaries that predate the op-log stop cleanly on the `FormatTooNew`\n  guard (step 2) rather than misreading. This is the intended, documented break.\n- No dual-write window: no residual LWW on legacy scalar keys.","state":"review","status":"open","title":"Op-log CRDT + derived cache (flagship)"}}}